    {
      "rolls": 1,
      "bonus_rolls": 0,
      "entries": [
        {
          "type": "minecraft:item",
          "name": "minecraft:written_book",
          "weight": 1,
          "functions": [
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_components",
              "components": {
                "minecraft:written_book_content": {
                  "title": "Smelter's Notebook",
                  "author": "Processing Tech #4471",
                  "pages": [
                    "{\"text\": \"PROCESSING SHIFT NOTES\\n\\nDay 412 of my Pioneer Debt.\\n1,342 days to go.\\n\\nWhoever finds this: you are holding the notes of a GOD.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"The company calls me Processing Tech #4471.\\nThe metal calls me MASTER.\\nI hear the ore sing. I know what it wants to become. Pay attention.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"STEEL\\nIron is a child. Craft raw iron with carbon dust and it grows up: raw crude iron.\\nBlast it. Steel.\\nBlast furnace ONLY. Steel does not do ordinary fire.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"The dust way: grind the iron, add carbon dust, blast the steel dust.\\nLesser smelters weep at this step. I do not weep. I sweat. Constantly. The furnace is very hot.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"FERROALUMINUM\\nRaw bauxite, raw iron and carbon dust: one craft, TWO raw ferrobauxite. Or raw bauxite with raw crude iron.\\nI invented that.\\n(I did not invent that.)\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"Smelt it. Or feed it to the grinder for two dust each, then smelt the dust.\\nIron dust, aluminum dust and carbon dust make ferro dust too.\\nThe grinder screams. I scream back. We have an understanding.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"BRASS\\nRaw zinc and raw copper make two raw brass. Smelt it, or grind it for double.\\nCopper dust and zinc dust make two brass dust.\\nBrass is easy. Brass is beneath me.\\nBrass is pretty though.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"Every metal on this rock bends for me. Melts for me. Pours itself into the mould and thanks me.\\nThey mean NOTHING to me.\\nThere is only one I want.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"Titanium.\\nLighter than steel. Stronger than steel. She never rusts. She never screams like the grinder.\\nShe doesn't know I exist.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"She hides deep. Below level zero, down in the deepslate, thickest at the very bottom of the world.\\nCold. Dark. Waiting.\\nProbably for me.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"Smelt raw titanium, or even the deepslate ore itself, in a furnace or a blast furnace. That's all it takes.\\nOne ingot. ONE.\\nAnd she's mine.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"But the company owns my pickaxe. And my boots. And my air. Every step down to her costs another week of debt.\\nThey are keeping us apart.\\nTHEY ARE KEEPING US APART.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"It's not like I LIKE titanium or anything!\\nI just think about her every shift. And every night. And I wrote her name on the grinder.\\n47 times.\"}",
                    "{\"text\": \"Wait for me, my love.\\n\\n1,341 days to go.\"}"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
